From 05645ff8d343b203eb0c4bdcd267453fe3154233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:54:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/35] watchdog: dw_wdt: Don't warn when the optional TOPs
 array is absent

snps,watchdog-tops is an optional property and most DTs (e.g. all
Rockchip ones) don't have it, so its absence is not worth a warning
on every boot. Keep warning when the property is present but invalid.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
index 39031445d754..9f3a3d1b05f4 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/dw_wdt.c
@@ -470,6 +470,8 @@ static int dw_wdt_init_timeouts(struct dw_wdt *dw_wdt, struct device *dev)
 	data = readl(dw_wdt->regs + WDOG_COMP_PARAMS_1_REG_OFFSET);
 	if (data & WDOG_COMP_PARAMS_1_USE_FIX_TOP) {
 		tops = dw_wdt_fix_tops;
+	} else if (!of_property_present(dev_of_node(dev), "snps,watchdog-tops")) {
+		tops = dw_wdt_fix_tops;
 	} else {
 		ret = of_property_read_variable_u32_array(dev_of_node(dev),
 			"snps,watchdog-tops", of_tops, DW_WDT_NUM_TOPS,
-- 
2.43.0

